Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">&#160;&#160;&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.31%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">$</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:14.53%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.75pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2024_4SUZ15s_Pkew4pHUZRUPZA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InventoryNet" scale="3" id="Tc_bszgk0V6ak2y1c9o2zBCCA_6_6">153,037</ix:nonFraction></span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:3.67%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">Finished goods inventory consigned to our distributors and agents throughout the Americas, Europe, and Asia was </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2025_Ddj8avuNXUekqecrPRoVuw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherInventoryMaterialsSuppliesAndMerchandiseUnderConsignment" scale="6" id="Narr_0TwXWdFzg0iB9m5P_IQEZA">10.6</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million and </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2024_4SUZ15s_Pkew4pHUZRUPZA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherInventoryMaterialsSuppliesAndMerchandiseUnderConsignment" scale="6" id="Narr_U3YhOlqX_kWtrPH_Er0YQg">10.3</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million as of October 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.</span></p></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">66</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="_Hlk217315947"></a><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_11_1_2024_To_10_31_2025_yHj0kCho6kqyjsmbpqPtIg" name="us-gaap:DebtDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_dxXJm0QTxkiKco2HP__XRg" continuedAt="Tb_dxXJm0QTxkiKco2HP__XRg_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-size:11pt;font-weight:bold;">4.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;CREDIT AGREEMENTS AND BORROWINGS</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:11pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">On December 31, 2018, we and our subsidiary Hurco B.V. entered into a credit agreement with Bank of America, N.A., as the lender, which was subsequently amended on each of March 13, 2020, December 23, 2020, December 17, 2021, January 4, 2023, and December 19, 2023 (as amended, the &#8220;2018 Credit Agreement&#8221;). The 2018 Credit Agreement provided for an unsecured revolving credit and letter of credit facility in a maximum aggregate amount of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2018_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2018Member_CTkyI6AnS0i1teS8KrRQvg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_IA4AvKIuM0idc2MniPJmSw">40.0</ix:nonFraction> million. The 2018 Credit Agreement provided that the maximum amount of outstanding letters of credit at any one time could not exceed $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2018_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2018Member_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_LetterOfCreditMember_a-Ff7r9m6kK-43x9jnDt7g" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_FbMIKhydH0WI4xLyUJW-DA">10.0</ix:nonFraction> million, the maximum amount of outstanding loans made to our subsidiary Hurco B.V. at any one time could not exceed $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2018_dei_LegalEntityAxis_hurc_HurcoBVMember_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2018Member_Tegoe9FuBEauCmI5WQG1IQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_EhjvVhmPEESktNo9gkTbmg">20.0</ix:nonFraction> million, and the maximum amount of all outstanding loans denominated in alternative currencies at any one time could not exceed $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2018_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2018Member_CTkyI6AnS0i1teS8KrRQvg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hurc:LineOfCreditMaximumBorrowingCapacityInAlternativeCurrencies" scale="6" id="Narr_KqOOiP9nVECEgmDKPSsitw">20.0</ix:nonFraction> million. The scheduled maturity date of the 2018 Credit Agreement was <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_12_31_2018_To_12_31_2018_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2018Member_2uD_QmGmKUWyjXSszFHUNg" format="ixt:date-monthname-day-year-en" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityExpirationDate1" id="Narr_ONVB_ZuNEE2FdlVwakO3zw">December 31, 2025</ix:nonNumeric>, and on that date, the 2018 Credit Agreement terminated in accordance with its terms. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">In March 2019, our wholly-owned subsidiaries in Taiwan, HML, and China, NHML, closed on uncommitted revolving credit facilities with maximum aggregate amounts of </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_TWD_pY0EOpFn0U6DZOVhHgp1nw" contextRef="As_Of_3_31_2019_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_hurc_TaiwanCreditFacilityMember_SPgkpXXaUUmpjNFkhiS2yA" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_WT393sAuw0GZDQ4QKIAbjw">150</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million New Taiwan Dollars and </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_a17_mUeMwEWSex1SK2KTAw" contextRef="As_Of_3_31_2019_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_hurc_ChinaCreditFacilityMember_h4ICn4__UEaT7zROceyo9A" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_x4XR3Yo_pEWXzuwOLhKvlg">32.5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million Chinese Yuan, respectively. As uncommitted facilities, both the Taiwan and China credit facilities were subject to review and termination by the respective underlying lending institution from time to time. In February and December 2023, NHML and HML, respectively, renewed the above-referenced credit facilities on substantially similar terms and identical maximum aggregate limits.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">As of October 31, 2025, our credit facilities consisted of a </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">&#8364;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_EUR_aS7WwVDrrkSY1e_3ELhvJg" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_DE_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_NdL29qwXbE6Fv0NGL8XfOg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_JsFzLtILGEO1XCaFwDOumQ">1.5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million revolving credit facility in Germany, the </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_TWD_pY0EOpFn0U6DZOVhHgp1nw" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2025_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_hurc_TaiwanCreditFacilityMember_C1tzWC5rwkOxnowiBSYH3Q" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_Sm6ezjO0Ekm2cQxmSHQS0w">150</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million New Taiwan Dollars Taiwan credit facility, the </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_a17_mUeMwEWSex1SK2KTAw" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2025_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_hurc_ChinaCreditFacilityMember_Q-moyOm_d0WF_ahF4RcBkQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_LVTROE5EfUSZQ11OS8GEHw">32.5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million Chinese Yuan China credit facility, and the </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2025_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2018Member_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_TkoZm0SvX0iEEa0eqriFkg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_vbsVjVXsTkKunUl6q6Dteg">40.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million revolving credit facility under the 2018 Credit Agreement. On December 31, 2025, the </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_TWD_pY0EOpFn0U6DZOVhHgp1nw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_hurc_TaiwanCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_U4BzwhvDykCItgJb9E4v9A" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_cJZ9bm0H1EiMn3CeUewuzQ">150</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million New Taiwan Dollars Taiwan credit facility, the </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_a17_mUeMwEWSex1SK2KTAw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_hurc_ChinaCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_vQWzYXZgvUaQKGEm8xgpyA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_tjePRzo5CU2p9o3spJ5J0g">32.5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million Chinese Yuan China credit facility and the </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2018Member_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_XZ_uM-38wUilbde0mLdcNA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_39Cr_QFJ1UaWxh0T5yR3XQ">40.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million revolving credit facility under the 2018 Credit Agreement terminated in accordance with their terms. </span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:11pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">We had <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2025_Ddj8avuNXUekqecrPRoVuw" decimals="-5" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:LineOfCredit" scale="6" id="Narr_fEVXMTrMnkSKQLBvpoydpg">no</ix:nonFraction> debt or <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_Y-yk6tDgw0qAuJc5GqPEWg;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">borrowings</span></span> outstanding under any of our credit facilities as of October 31, 2025, or December 31, 2025. As of October 31, 2025 we had an aggregate of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_10_31_2025_Ddj8avuNXUekqecrPRoVuw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityRemainingBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_4MgeM4WlNkysZbVIUBGyFQ">51.2</ix:nonFraction> million available for borrowing under our credit facilities.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">On January 5, 2026, we entered into a credit agreement with Bank of America, N.A., as the lender (the &#8220;2026 Credit Agreement&#8221;). The 2026 Credit Agreement provides for a secured revolving credit and letter of credit facility in a maximum aggregate amount of </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_E0wmZphdlkahYdRRFbQpbQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_qaq_mvgs_0OwoSPHPLTteg">20.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million. The 2026 Credit Agreement provides that the maximum amount of outstanding letters of credit at any one time may not exceed </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_LetterOfCreditMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_YGRDegqpZEqWkav96R4etg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_TtZB03c2LUirkqs9HkESGA">10.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million, and the maximum amount of all outstanding loans denominated in alternative currencies at any one time may not exceed </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="As_Of_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_E0wmZphdlkahYdRRFbQpbQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hurc:LineOfCreditMaximumBorrowingCapacityInAlternativeCurrencies" scale="6" id="Narr_z_ylKYZ5ZkOWFeAq-JcPTg">20.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million. Under the 2026 Credit Agreement, we are the borrower, and certain of our subsidiaries are guarantors. Our obligations under the 2026 Credit Agreement are secured by a security interest in substantially all of our personal property and substantially all of the personal property of each subsidiary guarantor. The scheduled maturity date of the 2026 Credit Agreement is December 31, 2026.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">Borrowings under the 2026 Credit Agreement bear interest at floating rates based on, at our option, either (i) a rate based upon the secured overnight financing rate (&#8220;SOFR&#8221;), the Sterling Overnight Index Average Reference Rate, the Euro Interbank Offering Rate, or another alternative currency-based rate approved by the lender, depending on the term of the loan and the currency in which such loan is denominated, plus </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_jj0rcDZiOUCx-E1zbbIpaA" contextRef="As_Of_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_E0wmZphdlkahYdRRFbQpbQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_CAMnq_DrUkauxoCz9KWGbA">2.50</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> per annum, or (ii) a base rate (which is the highest of (a) the federal funds rate plus </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_jj0rcDZiOUCx-E1zbbIpaA" contextRef="Duration_1_5_2026_To_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_FederalFundsEffectiveSwapRateMember_KpdXLunCeUGr8E7Xtb01RQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_SOTHXF582UGQLsKfuxNxeg">0.50</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-size:11pt;">, (b) the prime rate or (c) the one month SOFR-based rate plus </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_jj0rcDZiOUCx-E1zbbIpaA" contextRef="Duration_1_5_2026_To_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_SecuredOvernightFinancingRateSofrMember_ar-BtuAor062oADKRr4Rhw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_sZQafuYn_kyWCxnW9lg3ZQ">1.00</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-size:11pt;">), plus </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_jj0rcDZiOUCx-E1zbbIpaA" contextRef="Duration_1_5_2026_To_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_8ex5AIuTkU-J-icyAnVL-w" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_V6j0YWxD-UW3ZALLTKq6TQ">1.50</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> per annum. Outstanding letters of credit will carry an annual rate of </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_jj0rcDZiOUCx-E1zbbIpaA" contextRef="As_Of_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_LetterOfCreditMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_YGRDegqpZEqWkav96R4etg" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_2bz2JWTT7Ea7-A3VnpWe7A">2.50</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-size:11pt;">.</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">67</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_dxXJm0QTxkiKco2HP__XRg_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">The 2026 Credit Agreement contains customary affirmative and negative covenants and events of default, including covenants (1) restricting us from making certain investments, loans, advances and acquisitions (but permitting us to make investments in subsidiaries of up to </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="Duration_1_5_2026_To_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_8ex5AIuTkU-J-icyAnVL-w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hurc:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantAmountOfAllowableInvestment" scale="6" id="Narr__A-Hp8h56Eu8LaNsV03ioA">10.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million); (2) restricting us from making certain payments, including (a) cash dividends, except that we may pay cash dividends as long as immediately before and after giving effect to such payment, the sum of the unused amount of the commitments under the 2026 Credit Agreement plus our cash on hand is not less than </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="Duration_1_5_2026_To_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_8ex5AIuTkU-J-icyAnVL-w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hurc:LineOfCreditCovenantMinimumCashOnHandBeforeDividendsArePaid" scale="6" id="Narr_MGBGGweKpEen9Kjcxtbo5g">10.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million, we are in pro forma compliance with the maximum consolidated leverage ratio covenant as described below, and we are not in default before and after giving effect to such dividend payments and (b) payments made to repurchase shares of our common stock, except that we may repurchase shares of our common stock as long as we are not in default before and after giving effect to such repurchases and the aggregate amount of payments made by us for all such repurchases during any fiscal year does not exceed </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_-q6KwND1tUyIErqFk9amwg" contextRef="Duration_1_5_2026_To_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_8ex5AIuTkU-J-icyAnVL-w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hurc:LineOfCreditCovenantMaximumAnnualShareRepurchase" scale="6" id="Narr_dYqvSmRsrUaKSprpcoNRDw">10.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> million; and (3) requiring that we maintain a maximum consolidated leverage ratio of total debt to EBITDA no greater than </span><span style="font-size:11pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_jj0rcDZiOUCx-E1zbbIpaA" contextRef="Duration_1_5_2026_To_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_8ex5AIuTkU-J-icyAnVL-w" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hurc:LineOfCreditCovenantMaximumConsolidatedLeverageRatio" scale="-2" id="Narr_w-HW-oZAIEKVCjEdwhT5ag">2.00</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;"> to 1.00, with EBITDA defined as the greater of (i) consolidated EBITDA for the most recently completed measurement period and (ii) </span><span style="font-size:11pt;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_cK0tCHROTEui2Cyp4lJA6w" contextRef="Duration_1_5_2026_To_1_5_2026_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreementAxis_hurc_LineOfCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_8ex5AIuTkU-J-icyAnVL-w" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hurc:LineOfCreditCovenantEarningsBeforeIncomeTaxDepreciationAndAmortizationPerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_ub-XZhnpyE-v5UjB5E_0qA">1.00</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-size:11pt;">. We may use the proceeds from advances under the 2026 Credit Agreement for general corporate purposes.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">The maximum consolidated leverage ratio covenant effectively prohibits us from borrowing any amounts under the 2026 Credit Agreement when our consolidated EBITDA for the most recently completed measurement period is negative. As of the date we entered into the 2026 Credit Agreement, the most recently completed measurement period was our fiscal year ended October 31, 2025, during which our consolidated EBITDA was negative. In order to borrow in compliance with the maximum consolidated leverage ratio covenant set forth above, we are effectively prohibited from borrowing under the 2026 Credit Agreement until we have positive consolidated EBITDA for our most recently completed four fiscal quarters. </span></p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;font-weight:bold;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><a id="_9951983c_e99a_4fb0_b576_588e3dac3fd6"></a><a id="Tc_9YJkFKdlR0e_o1znMng8zA_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_1-ibz9VjLUKafOboOCjkHA_1_8"></a><a id="Tc_ykFyQ1GY40OusnDPIeqG8w_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_Q52HnMkii0uEqES7PctNLQ_2_5"></a><a id="Tc_yFXADrDIZ0udVDx01FDeoA_2_8"></a><a id="Tc_GUr8f6pwS0qA7z3xEXKM5g_2_11"></a><a id="Tc_k7nokiZYhkS0n3_Hfcb1vA_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_zi_VgX763EC-L_89usI7eQ_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_oBY-qWWrokWJl7jzO5korg_4_2"></a><a id="Tc_mBJ2SgoYBEe2tt2PRHF23w_4_5"></a><a id="Tc_fHnEDR32mEaMOrpKykodPA_4_8"></a><a id="Tc_8DXi-qNgikGDvekzIb2PdA_4_9"></a><a id="Tc_ry5PIl7VY0ykwfAtmXK6ow_4_11"></a><a id="Tc_pozMTp_ubEyksLQMS2WGTw_4_12"></a><a id="Tc_VClcjEpM3kOih7TUHHU-qg_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_xs8NSE9opUSsJqdZfCyrKw_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_Jq4rZhCv-U-jyvDi58sDRg_7_2"></a><a id="Tc_Z48AKuEmS02AOTk-y3pCeg_7_5"></a><a id="Tc_FwMG6fASakarwqIIJcL7pQ_7_8"></a><a id="Tc_L32hmR0pcU6GYpUu76Xjfw_7_11"></a><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_11_1_2024_To_10_31_2025_yHj0kCho6kqyjsmbpqPtIg" name="us-gaap:FinancialInstrumentsDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_kirIFsOyKUGgulz3Twj-aw" continuedAt="Tb_kirIFsOyKUGgulz3Twj-aw_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-size:11pt;font-weight:bold;">5.</b><span style="font-size:11pt;">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span><b style="font-size:11pt;font-weight:bold;">FINANCIAL INSTRUMENTS</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-size:11pt;">Estimated Fair Value of Financial Instruments</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">FASB fair value guidance establishes a three&#8211;tier fair value hierarchy, which categorizes the inputs used in measuring fair value. These tiers include: Level 1, defined as observable inputs, such as quoted prices in active markets; Level 2, defined as inputs other than quoted prices in active markets that are either directly or indirectly observable; and Level 3, defined as unobservable inputs for which little or no market data exists, therefore requiring an entity to develop its own assumptions.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">The carrying amounts for cash and cash equivalents approximate their fair values due to the short maturity of these instruments, and such instruments meet the Level 1 criteria of the three&#8211;tier fair value hierarchy discussed above. The carrying amount of short-term debt approximates fair value due to the variable rate of interest and the short-term nature of the instrument.</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_11_1_2024_To_10_31_2025_yHj0kCho6kqyjsmbpqPtIg" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfFairValueAssetsAndLiabilitiesMeasuredOnRecurringBasisTableTextBlock" id="Tb_LfTQtyVpRUODUhOxaowhkA" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;">In accordance with this guidance, the following table represents the fair value hierarchy for our financial assets and liabilities measured at fair value as of October 31, 2025 and 2024 (in thousands):</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;margin-left:-0.6799927%;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:101.35%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:23.96%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.23%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.93%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:14.28%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.23%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.68%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:14.52%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><di